    /// P\\*A\\*P^{T} = L\\*D\\*L^{T}
    /// $$
    ///
    /// If input parameter `uplo` is [`cublasFillMode_t::CUBLAS_FILL_MODE_UPPER`], only upper triangular part of `A` is processed, and replaced by upper triangular factor `U` and block diagonal matrix `D`.
    /// $$
    /// P\\*A\\*P^{T} = U\\*D\\*U^{T}
    /// $$
    ///
    /// The user has to provide working space which is pointed by input parameter `work`. The input parameter `lwork` is size of the working space, and it is returned by `sytrf_bufferSize()`. Please note that the size in bytes of the working space is equal to `sizeof(&lt;type>) * lwork`. When no pivoting is performed, the other triangular part of the input matrix `A` is used as workspace.
    ///
    /// If Bunch-Kaufman factorization failed, i.e. `A` is singular. The output parameter `devInfo = i` would indicate `D(i,i)=0`.
    ///
